	<key>readme</key>
	<string># grabLocations

Collect the locations of your Apple Calendar events over the next few days and open them as a Google Maps directions route.

## Setup
- **Calendar**: one or more Calendar names, comma-separated (e.g. `Work, Family`)
- **Days**: how many days ahead to look (default `7`)

Alfred needs **Full Access** to Calendars: System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Calendars › Alfred › Full Access. If it is missing, the workflow shows a message; press ↩ on it to open that settings pane.

Requires Python 3 (`xcode-select --install` if `python3` is missing).

## Usage
Type `grablocation` to list a route per calendar, plus a combined route when you list several calendars (routes are split into batches of 10 stops). Add a US ZIP code (e.g. `grablocation 02139`) to keep only locations in that ZIP. Press ↩ to open the route in Google Maps.

Created in response to https://www.alfredforum.com/topic/20087-search-for-multiple-address-in-googlemaps-to-make-a-route/</string>
